; A word that names no directive is never dispatched, even when an
; expression definition gives it a meaning: `define` makes a function,
; not a directive.  With an argument it is an unrecognized source line;
; without one it is reported as missing its argument, since only
; comment, end, python and test take none.  A word directive that needs
; an argument reports it missing, and the legacy `Y` does the same.

define foo=1

foo bar

foo

year

Y

end

